WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.184 --> 00:00:02.598
- I feel like Mexican chips and flavors,

00:00:02.598 --> 00:00:05.083
10 times better than
American chips and flavors.

00:00:05.944 --> 00:00:07.560
- Smells like a fart a little bit.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.104
(flamenco music)
(both laughing)

00:00:11.104 --> 00:00:12.390
- [Both] Churrimais

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.945
- Con limoncito.

00:00:13.945 --> 00:00:16.105
- Churima, so it's like
little churros with lime.

00:00:16.105 --> 00:00:17.429
- (gasps) Oh.
- Sounds delicious.

00:00:17.429 --> 00:00:19.518
- A lot of spices visible
on the chip, which I like.

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:21.445
- A lot of spices visible in my nose.

00:00:21.445 --> 00:00:22.522
- The lime might be a little much.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.667
I could do without the lime.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:24.975
- Yeah, I mean, I feel that about

00:00:24.975 --> 00:00:26.260
most lime chips.
- Agreed.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.040
- Ooh!

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.036
- Whoa.
- Flavor sensation.

00:00:30.036 --> 00:00:31.577
- That is a punch of lime.

00:00:31.577 --> 00:00:33.252
- Actually, it's delicious.
- Muy bien.

00:00:33.252 --> 00:00:34.859
- You know what it's
like, it's like a shrunken

00:00:34.859 --> 00:00:36.585
voodoo head version of a churro.

00:00:36.585 --> 00:00:38.644
- You're right, this is a churro for mice.

00:00:38.644 --> 00:00:39.643
(man laughing)

00:00:40.289 --> 00:00:42.220
- [Both] Gansito.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.192
- It has a cute little,
uh, who's that guy again?

00:00:45.192 --> 00:00:46.446
- Is that Howard the Duck?

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:49.301
- I love how alternative he is.

00:00:49.301 --> 00:00:51.609
He's like, "I'm a cool duck.

00:00:51.609 --> 00:00:53.226
"I'm a duck from the streets."

00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:55.021
- This is like a Mexican Twinkie.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.414
- Yes.

00:00:56.414 --> 00:00:58.265
- I do like the weight
here, like this is a--

00:00:58.265 --> 00:01:00.024
- It's a good snack.
- It's a hefty snack.

00:01:00.024 --> 00:01:01.567
- Cheers.
- Boom.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.653
- Oh, yeah!

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.544
- [Man] I love this.
- [Woman] I don't like it.

00:01:07.544 --> 00:01:08.590
- Give me your half.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:09.595
- I don't like it.

00:01:09.595 --> 00:01:11.292
- I don't like the jam.

00:01:11.292 --> 00:01:13.435
- I didn't like it the first
second I opened my mouth.

00:01:13.435 --> 00:01:14.505
(man laughing)

00:01:15.122 --> 00:01:17.273
- Sabritones. Did I get that right?

00:01:17.273 --> 00:01:19.277
- This is gonna be (bleep)in' delicious.

00:01:19.277 --> 00:01:21.785
That's a puffed chip that tastes like

00:01:21.785 --> 00:01:23.241
chili and lime, let's eat it.

00:01:23.241 --> 00:01:25.779
- Look at all the spices on this chip,

00:01:25.779 --> 00:01:27.613
they are leavin' nothin' at home,

00:01:27.613 --> 00:01:29.586
they're like goin' all out every time.

00:01:29.586 --> 00:01:32.646
- Oh, fun, it's a party.

00:01:32.646 --> 00:01:34.137
- When you first take a bite, it's like

00:01:34.137 --> 00:01:37.318
"This is popcorn," and
then you get the spice.

00:01:37.318 --> 00:01:39.478
And then, you get the lime.

00:01:39.478 --> 00:01:42.317
- It's a three sensation experience.

00:01:43.448 --> 00:01:46.870
- Cacahuates peanuts, Japones style.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.131
- Why'd you say it like that? (laughs)

00:01:48.131 --> 00:01:49.694
- You brought us to a Mexican taste test

00:01:49.694 --> 00:01:52.923
and gave us Japanese peanuts?
That shit (bleep)ed up.

00:01:52.923 --> 00:01:55.034
- Can I just tell you,
it smells like peanuts,

00:01:55.034 --> 00:01:58.122
but it also smells like
grass in the summer.

00:01:59.748 --> 00:02:01.164
- It smells like grass in the summer.

00:02:01.164 --> 00:02:03.557
- (bleep) right, doesn't it
smell like grass in the summer?

00:02:03.557 --> 00:02:04.811
- And what was the other thing you said?

00:02:04.811 --> 00:02:05.912
- [Woman] Peanuts.
- [Man] Yeah!

00:02:05.912 --> 00:02:07.305
(woman laughing)
Dead on.

00:02:07.305 --> 00:02:08.465
- They're, like, in a thing.

00:02:08.465 --> 00:02:09.471
- Yeah, they don't really--

00:02:09.471 --> 00:02:10.686
- [Man] They look like rocks.
- [Woman] They don't look

00:02:10.686 --> 00:02:11.901
like food, yeah, rocks.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:13.132
- They look like cartoon food.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.486
(crunching)

00:02:14.486 --> 00:02:15.527
- Damn!

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.425
- [Man] This is delicious.
- [Woman] I'm into them.

00:02:18.425 --> 00:02:19.725
- I don't know what it is.

00:02:19.725 --> 00:02:20.964
- What is on you, nut?

00:02:20.964 --> 00:02:22.319
- That's a great crunch,
I don't understand

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:23.804
what that crunch is.
- Yeah.

00:02:23.804 --> 00:02:25.678
- They put something on
the outside of the peanut?

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.325
(loud crunching)

00:02:27.325 --> 00:02:31.435
A ha, there's a crisp on this peanut.

00:02:33.081 --> 00:02:35.138
- [Man] Rancheritos.
- [Woman] Yeah,

00:02:35.138 --> 00:02:36.778
it's got a cowboy hat
and a bandana, ranch.

00:02:36.778 --> 00:02:37.976
- Yee haw.

00:02:37.976 --> 00:02:40.528
- This is Cool Ranch,
maybe, but the real ranch.

00:02:40.528 --> 00:02:43.310
- Oh, it's just a Dorito.
(crunching)

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:45.074
It's the exact same thing.

00:02:45.074 --> 00:02:46.607
- This is 100% Cool Ranch Dorito, like--

00:02:46.607 --> 00:02:48.116
- These are Cool Ranch Doritos cut into

00:02:48.116 --> 00:02:49.672
a different shape and
put in a different bag.

00:02:49.672 --> 00:02:51.320
- Kinda barbecue-y.
- Yeah.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.689
- But like, real barbecue, like

00:02:53.689 --> 00:02:56.127
the, the smoke from the barbecue.

00:02:56.127 --> 00:02:57.450
- Why do we have to have triangles?

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.091
Why can't we have strips?

00:02:59.091 --> 00:03:00.529
- Strips seem a lot more efficient,

00:03:01.529 --> 00:03:04.231
and I feel like, just at first glance,

00:03:04.231 --> 00:03:06.250
a lot less crumbly in
there than a Dorito bag.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:10.151
- I feel like Mexicans like spicy flavors

00:03:10.151 --> 00:03:14.377
like chili and lime, and
Americans like mild-ass flavors

00:03:14.377 --> 00:03:18.673
like cheese and sour cream.
(woman on left laughing)

00:03:18.673 --> 00:03:21.622
Or like, the mildest
salsa that exists, right?

00:03:21.622 --> 00:03:23.023
- Yes, like tomatoes.

00:03:23.023 --> 00:03:24.230
- Yeah (laughs), they're like,

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.766
"No, no salsa, just, do you
have a paste of tomatoes?"

00:03:27.766 --> 00:03:29.108
(woman on left laughing)

